From c9301f83ed662321188ca67420751dfa0eb442bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 20:04:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ios): wire flutter_native_splash to replace 68-byte stub
 launch images
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Xcode rejects iOS archives because Runner/Assets.xcassets/LaunchImage.imageset
contains the default Flutter stub PNGs (68 bytes each — 1px transparent
placeholders shipped by 'flutter create'). Without real launch images,
'flutter build ipa --release' fails App Store validation.

Adds flutter_native_splash ^2.4.4 to dev_dependencies and a config block
that:
  - Uses the existing assets/images/app-logo.png (1261x1261 RGBA, the
    same brand mark used elsewhere in the app) as the centered splash.
  - Renders on a warm parchment background (#FAF6F0) that matches the
    Legacy Table landing-page palette.
  - Targets both iOS and Android in the same pass — Android currently
    ships with default placeholders too, so this fixes both.

After applying this patch, run:
    cd mobile
    flutter pub get
    dart run flutter_native_splash:create

That regenerates:
  ios/Runner/Assets.xcassets/LaunchImage.imageset/LaunchImage{,@2x,@3x}.png
  ios/Runner/Base.lproj/LaunchScreen.storyboard
  android/app/src/main/res/drawable-*/launch_image.png
  android/app/src/main/res/values/styles.xml (background color)

Then re-run 'flutter build ipa --release' — the archive will pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mobile/pubspec.yaml | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mobile/pubspec.yaml b/mobile/pubspec.yaml
index 850e21c..2ba8989 100644
--- a/mobile/pubspec.yaml
+++ b/mobile/pubspec.yaml
@@ -61,6 +61,7 @@ dependencies:
 
 dev_dependencies:
   flutter_launcher_icons: ^0.14.4
+  flutter_native_splash: ^2.4.4
   flutter_test:
     sdk: flutter
 
@@ -158,3 +159,23 @@ flutter_launcher_icons:
   image_path: "assets/images/app-icon.png"
   adaptive_icon_background: "#000000"
   adaptive_icon_foreground: "assets/images/app-icon.png"
+
+# Native splash / launch screen.
+# Run `dart run flutter_native_splash:create` after editing this block to
+# regenerate the iOS LaunchImage.imageset + LaunchScreen.storyboard and
+# the Android drawable-* splash assets from the source image below.
+#
+# Without this, iOS ships with the default 68-byte stub PNGs in
+# Runner/Assets.xcassets/LaunchImage.imageset and Xcode rejects the
+# archive with "missing launch image."
+flutter_native_splash:
+  # Warm parchment background — matches the Legacy Table brand palette.
+  color: "#FAF6F0"
+  # Centered logo. Same source asset Flutter ships from elsewhere in the
+  # app, so the splash and the in-app brand mark match exactly.
+  image: assets/images/app-logo.png
+  # Platforms — generate for both. (Android also currently uses default
+  # placeholders; this fixes both in one pass.)
+  ios: true
+  android: true
+  web: false
-- 
